Background and definitions. A pre-NQ manifold is a non-negatively graded supermanifold equipped with a graded symplectic form of degree 2 together with a degree-1 vector field Q whose square need not vanish; when Q² = 0 the structure is an NQ manifold and recovers a Courant algebroid. Pre-NQ manifolds of degree 2 over a smooth manifold provide a local model for the gauge structure of Double Field Theory (DFT): the standard "doubled" Courant-algebroid-like bracket, the strong constraint, and the C-bracket all arise from derived brackets associated with Q.

Topological T-duality (in the sense of Bouwknegt–Evslin–Mathai or Bunke–Schick) associates to a pair (M, G) consisting of a principal torus bundle M → M₀ together with an abelian bundle gerbe G of Dixmier–Douady class h ∈ H³(M, ℤ) a T-dual pair (M̃, G̃) over the same base M₀, together with the correspondence space M ×_{M₀} M̃ on which the pullbacks of G and G̃ become isomorphic. By a "non-trivially fibered spacetime" we mean a smooth manifold M which is the total space of a non-trivial principal torus bundle over a base M₀, equipped with a gerbe G of non-trivial Dixmier–Douady class.

Known global constructions. (i) For geometric T-duality on principal torus bundles, a globally defined pre-NQ manifold encoding DFT has been built on the correspondence space M ×_{M₀} M̃ equipped with the pullback of both G and G̃; this construction takes the topological T-duality data as input. (ii) For DFT on group manifolds, a globally defined pre-NQ formulation has been given. In both cases the correspondence space, or its analogue, is supplied externally rather than produced by the pre-NQ formalism itself.

Problem. Construct, or prove the impossibility of, a single global pre-NQ manifold P assigned to every "T-dualizable background" (M, G) — a non-trivially fibered spacetime M with gerbe G admitting a topological T-dual — such that:

(a) P is built canonically from the data (M, G) alone, without taking the T-dual (M̃, G̃) or the correspondence space M ×_{M₀} M̃ as part of the input;

(b) P globalizes the local pre-NQ model of DFT (i.e., locally on patches it reduces to the standard degree-2 graded symplectic pre-NQ structure used to derive the C-bracket and strong constraint of DFT);

(c) the topological data of the T-dual gerbe G̃ and of the correspondence space are recovered from P (for instance via canonical transformations of the graded symplectic structure or via reductions of P) rather than being duplicated as input;

(d) the construction specializes to the existing global pre-NQ models in the geometric (principal torus bundle) case and in the group-manifold case.

Decide whether such a globalization exists in general, and if so, provide an explicit construction; if not, identify the obstruction.

